1:# Theming — `--g-*` tokens, `ThemeProvider`, branding, custom themes
2-
3-> **Source of truth:** this is a verbatim copy of
4-> [`@gravity-ui/uikit`'s `docs/theming.md`](https://github.com/gravity-ui/uikit/blob/main/docs/theming.md).
--
11-> here, prefer the version-matched source over this snapshot.
12-
13-For the **traps** — what goes wrong when theming a Gravity UI app (partial
14:overrides, brand-on-brand contrast, a `ThemeProvider` that themes the whole page, the
15-customization ladder) — see [`../rules/hallucination-traps.md`](../rules/hallucination-traps.md).
16-That file complements this reference rather than duplicating it.
17-
--
26-Everything is driven by CSS custom properties prefixed with `--g-*`. There is no runtime styling API you need to call — you set variables and components pick them up.
27-
28-```tsx
29:import {ThemeProvider, Button} from '@gravity-ui/uikit';
30-import '@gravity-ui/uikit/styles/fonts.css';
31-import '@gravity-ui/uikit/styles/styles.css';
32-
33-export const App = () => (
34:  <ThemeProvider theme="system">
35-    <Button view="action">Branded button</Button>
36:  </ThemeProvider>
37-);
38-```
39-
40-## How theming works
41-
42:All variables live on the root class `.g-root`, which `ThemeProvider` assigns to `<body>` by
43-default (change the target with the `scoped` prop). Color variables additionally live on a
44-per-theme class `.g-root_theme_{themeName}`, so switching the theme swaps one set of values for
45-another.
46-
47-```
48:.g-root                      → structural tokens (spacing, typography metrics, border radius)
49-.g-root_theme_light          → color tokens for the light theme
50-.g-root_theme_dark           → color tokens for the dark theme
51-```
--
64-| `light-hc` | Light, high-contrast (accessibility) |
65-| `dark-hc`  | Dark, high-contrast (accessibility)  |
66-
67:Select the theme via `ThemeProvider`:
68-
69-```tsx
70:<ThemeProvider theme="dark">{...}</ThemeProvider>
71-```
72-
73-The default is `"system"`, which follows the OS color-scheme preference and resolves to `light`
74-or `dark`. You can control what `system` resolves to with `systemLightTheme` / `systemDarkTheme`.
75:Read or switch the theme at runtime with the `useTheme` / `useThemeValue` hooks.
76-
77-## Color token layers
78-
--
81-
82-### Private tokens
83-
84:`--g-color-private-*` are the raw palette — the actual RGB values, organized by hue and by a
85-numeric scale. They exist so the semantic layer has something to point at. **Do not use them
86-directly in application code**; they are an implementation detail and can change.
87-
--
90-
91-Two flavors per step:
